# Result/Benchmark Markdown: Clean Numbers Only

When writing or editing any results, benchmark, or comparison markdown file:

- Lead with the numbers. A short header (branch/commit, image, command) plus the comparison table(s) is the whole file.
- NO prose verdicts, NO "Notes/caveats" sections, NO interpretation paragraphs, NO emojis, NO motivational filler.
- Put deltas in the table itself if useful, not in sentences.
- If the user wants analysis, they will ask. Default to numbers only.
